> 
> -Is there a better starting strategy with an orcish ranger?

Looks fine to me. But don't waste your arrows on gnomes. That's what
your pet is for. Or use the gnomes for dagger training. A bunch of
daggers is great spare ammo that never gets lost. Oh, and try to get
some poisoned arrows off those uruks (or alternatively a potion of
sickness). Most big animals are not poison resistant, so even your
mastodon would have died after ~10 arrows, that is 4 turns at high
enough bow skill. And of course: use your displacement, keep moving and
keep your distance.
 
